WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.030
Having returned to Kasarelia,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.460
Üso senses that Katejina has grown fond of Cronicle.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.700
As does Cronicle.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:40.360
However, for Katejina, who intended to spy for Üso and the others,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.300
the warmth of Kasarelia made her feel jealousy.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.900
VIVID! SHRIKE TEAM

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.930
"Vivid! Shrike Team".

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:50.300
VIVID! SHRIKE TEAM

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.500
What is it, Marbet?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.400
If you've got a problem with me, just come out with it.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.960
Get me a B5 screw!

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.000
Are you sure?

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:17.630
Could you stop playing junior tactician, please?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.360
Shouldn't you hurry home? Don't you have your own unit?

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.600
Yeah, but you've been tight-lipped since yesterday and it's got me curious.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.100
Üso, we're all set here.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.600
We'll discuss this later!

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.660
Got that, Marbet?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.200
Are you sure about this, Miss Marbet?

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.800
Are the joint sections okay?

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:40.960
Fine.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.260
The unit Mr. Oliver's meeting is called the Shrike Team, right?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.300
Quiet! Oliver has the details. Ask him!

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.260
It's like they're practicing having a lover's quarrel...

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.600
Mr. Romero, can I link with the Boots now?

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.300
Sure. Do it!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.600
We've finally gotten orders from Jinn Jahannam!

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.460
Jinn Jahannam?

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:12.700
The leader of the League Militaire. Why?

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:17.060
Well, League Militaire means "holy alliance", right?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.000
You're well-informed.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.260
It's ancient Roman, right?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.960
But, Jahannam means "hell,"

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.200
and a "jinn" is the name of a monster that lives in it, right?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.630
Do you know what it's called in Hindu?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.700
It's called "Uso," right?

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.400
You're doing it, huh?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.360
Nearly done.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.630
People need names like that to inspire them, right?

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.560
Is that person in D.D.?

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.530
No idea.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.760
We're just resisting the Zanscare who have come to steal Europe.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.430
If we do that, maybe the Earth Federation...

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.960
...will finally get around to taking a stand against them.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.400
Is Shrike Team coming to D.D. as well?

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:00.130
Do you have a problem with Shrike Team, Marbet?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.560
B,L,E... T,O...

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.630
D point, D point, J, I, N.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.230
One moment, please.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.130
Go to it.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.030
Combined with the vocal track,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.860
it decodes as "Gather at D.D. within 28 hours. Jinn Jahannam."

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.530
All right. D.D. can only be the old City of Dresden.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.060
Doubtless.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:35.830
Lt. Dupré, when did you get a copy of the complete works of McKinley?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:39.330
Heh... Karaoke is my hobby.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.760
You're hesitant to accept my assistance. Why?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.960
One must command from the lead to distinguish oneself, right?

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.760
My job isn't to just simply remain planted at an office desk.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.860
I know how you feel.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.500
It goes with being promoted out of the cockpit.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.200
Right, which is why I'd like to borrow your Tomliats for my unit.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.430
Damn you, Pippiniden.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.900
When I get results, I'll have you thrown out of here.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:21.000
Kwan Lee, Lupe Cineau, the resistance forces are en route to D.D.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.130
We'll suppress them and help Lt. Dupré.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.360
I'm gonna win again.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.660
Don't bet on it.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.260
Üso, come play poker with us.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.100
No, thanks. I'm fine.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.530
Okay, let's see 'em.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.230
A full house?

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.900
Hey Odelo, it just doesn't add up.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.060
Huh? What?

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.800
Do you really think Miss Katejina is going to Arti Gibraltar?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.500
She said she was going with that Cronicle guy.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.830
Besides that, what if someone else intercepted...

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.960
...that coded message from Jinn Jahannam?

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.130
What do you mean?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.330
D.D. isn't code. You can tell it's Dresden just from the spelling.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:19.860
There's another way of reading that message,

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.660
which is why we're headed the opposite way from Dresden.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.300
If the League Militaire can do that,

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.160
couldn't the Largaine forces run a diversion of their own?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.900
Would you shut up? Who cares if they do?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.830
Sorry, I'm overthinking this.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.930
I know I need to think this over by myself.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:44.800
Haro!

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.230
Haro! Haro! Haro! Haro!

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.160
Shut up!

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.860
Haro. Haro.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:52.930
Enough, okay?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.960
It hurts!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.560
Even trees have their own quirks.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.660
That's what you get for recklessly trying to cut one down.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.660
Go home and get that treated.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:05.930
O-Okay.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.230
Mother!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.030
Uh-oh, better get that disinfected.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.960
Üso, you're a big boy now.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.030
You need to be a little more observant.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.000
All they ever did was lecture me.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.200
Of course! If Largaine runs a diversion operation...

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:34.560
We should probably try taking this route.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:38.760
But if the attack force from Largaine headed for D.D. tries...

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.200
...to go to Arti Gibraltar...

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.900
...and we try taking this course,

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.900
then that force could end up dragging us down.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.030
Üso?

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.660
That's dangerous!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.360
If you go out, take me with you.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.200
How can you say that? There might be a battle!

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:06.200
Just as likely here on the Camion. I'm worried about you.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.630
Aren't you scared?

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:16.330
If I ask the old men, they'll just say no.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.200
Hang on a sec.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.830
Haro!

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:27.360
Okay, watch your step and just come on over.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:35.260
You did it!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:38.560
Careful!

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.430
Sure thing.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.360
Odelo, I'm loading the missiles.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.100
Ask Suzy to help, too.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.960
Suzy! Suzy, where are you? Give me a hand!

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.330
I'm glad there doesn't seem to be a problem in the joints.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:03.260
The real question is if the Minovsky flight functions will work.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:06.460
Since we've successfully docked in mid-air,

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.260
our initial estimates show...

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.430
Haro, where's Üso?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:12.900
Haro!

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.400
Don't fall.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.130
Haro!

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:17.860
Üso, we're clear.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.230
Suzy!

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.260
For crying out loud...

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.300
If you want out, now's the time.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.500
Don't worry.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.400
Why's the main engine on?

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:46.030
Üso, what are you doing? Where are you going?!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.930
Don't! Flying out on your own will be too obvious!

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.430
I'm headed for Arti Gibraltar to follow the enemy!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.330
I'm playing along with their plan!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.760
You're not equipped for that!

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.960
Üso, not now!

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.260
This is bad, Romero.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:07.530
What the...

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.700
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.530
Üso's tendency to overthink things. I hope this doesn't backfire on him.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.460
Lt. Dupré, possible fighter craft, closing.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.760
And they're not headed for point D.D.?

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.500
Right.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.660
It's so pretty, Karl. Do you see it?

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:42.960
Üso and I have never seen a field of flowers together like this!

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:48.400
What?

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.760
Well, either we've been tricked or they're right on schedule.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.400
It's the enemy.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.130
The enemy?

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:00.130
So, is it a second diversion or an ambush?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.030
It's parts from the white suit! Capture it!

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.060
The enemy wants to capture this machine undamaged!

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.030
If we're captured, we can't go looking for your mom!

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.600
Brace yourself!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.830
Hang in there, Shahkti.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:49.430
Your body will be buried amidst the scent of lilacs.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:50.860
That won't be so bad.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.030
I can't fight with Shahkti here!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.500
My own son is 16.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:09.360
That was a child! Just a child!

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.630
Don't shoot it down! Capture it! Is that clear?!

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.400
Stop, please! I have civilians aboard!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.160
More of them!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:30.900
Is it not maneuvering as well as it should because a child is operating it?

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:35.460
But why is a child piloting League Militaire mobile suit parts?

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.030
I won't see Miss Katejina again. Did I just fall for their feint?!

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:41.660
Can't you stop this, Üso?

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.530
I'm sorry this happened.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.960
What's wrong? Don't worry about me!

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:05.860
Either way, getting the white suit's parts...

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.000
...was worth going out here for.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.830
Were they trying to rendezvous with this unit?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.960
Friendly reinforcements have arrived! But from where?

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.060
Huh? They look like Gundams.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.960
Is it that Shrike Team Mr. Oliver mentioned?

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.160
Of course! Shrike Team!

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.960
Of all the selfish stunts! You idiot!

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.630
Mr. Oliver followed us from the Camion!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.830
Üso, dock now and help out!

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:25.560
Don't cry.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.030
There, Karl is clear.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.930
Take another step.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.060
What?

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:35.360
Why is there a baby with him?!

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:43.330
It's Shrike Team. Shahkti, are you all right?

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:52.060
Nice work, Shahkti. Now stand back from the plane.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.130
Don't come out of the woods!

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.230
Right!

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.400
Take this!

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.230
What? A pistol?

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:01.760
It's a flare gun! You have two shots!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:02.830
Right.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:04.700
Quiet!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.630
Üso Ewin, here I go!

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:30.160
Nice machine.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.000
Shrike Team, go!!!

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:38.960
Does that mobile suit unit plan on holding nothing back?!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:41.460
Assume quick attack formation!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.800
You know a mid-air docking is easy for the enemy to target, right?

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:00.130
Mr. Oliver, please give me that Hanger!

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.060
Docking, complete! That was fast!

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:25.930
Why, you...!

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.600
Karl?

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:58.530
That... wasn't Üso.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:12.560
I blew up its main engine.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.360
If you stop, you'll get killed!

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.660
Retreat or attack! Make up your mind!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:22.960
Another lady pilot?

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.260
You can't fight a war by yourself.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.030
What?!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:58.930
You can't tell from the explosions which are enemies and which are allies.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:01.130
Shrike Team's still okay.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.800
I can't see anything!

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:06.860
The radio's completely useless! Lots of Minovsky particles out there.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.830
Another one. Are you sure they're okay?

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.630
This mobile suit team...

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.960
The enemy's way too reckless!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.330
Aren't they amateurs?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:24.130
No, these Gundam replicas know hand-to-hand combat well!

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:32.200
The Camion!

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:41.330
Shahkti! Put Karlmann down!

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:42.830
Sure.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.260
You know what's up with Üso and the others?

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:51.500
N... No. Mr. Oliver arrived, but I...

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.160
You ran away by yourself?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:56.460
Just get her aboard the Camion and have Leonid take a look at her.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.300
Right.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:03.760
Ü-Üso... Never mind me... Fight!

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:05.400
Shahkti's...

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:12.960
Damn!

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:16.330
Mahalia! I'll save you!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.900
There you are!

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.160
Wow.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:28.960
Incredible...

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.160
All of a sudden, I don't see any friendly units!

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.060
How many enemies are left? Just them?

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:44.960
No need to pursue, Junko.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:55.560
Mr. Victory Pilot, you've got good skills.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.300
I can't believe you disabled two Tomliats without blowing them up.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:01.300
It... It was nothing.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:04.630
I could only do it because you all were here with me.

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.700
How is she?

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:11.760
A little scratched up. Let's leave her to rest.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.530
Right.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:14.930
They're in sight.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.730
Oliver's Shrike Team?

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:18.300
There's six of them, huh?

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:21.600
Along with the Victory and Mr. Oliver's core fighter.

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:25.960
Although the setters that carried the Gun EZs aren't armed.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.600
The ability to transport is useful in war.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.800
I like your lipstick today.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:40.730
Thank you.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.730
And thank you for before.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:43.530
It was nothing.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.360
I can't believe it, though.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:46.630
Sorry.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.300
It really was this kid?

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.130
There's no one else here.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.560
Thanks for all you did.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.330
Same to you. You helped us.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.660
So, this kid really is a pilot, huh?

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.160
Yeah, he's got good sense.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.400
Did you cut your hair because of a broken heart?

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:03.360
Hardly!

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:06.300
Cony, are your freckles lighter now?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:10.430
Peggie, they say this kid is the Victory pilot.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:14.400
Are you telling us he's a Newtype, Commander Oliver Inoe?

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.460
Shrike Team are all women.

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:20.030
Regardless of where we go from D.D.,

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:22.930
we won't know what'll happen until we get there.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.830
Since production of the Victory type is proceeding,

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:28.030
we shouldn't have a problem with firepower.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:31.630
Which means we're trying an all-out attack on Largaine?

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:33.460
Acting like such a ladies man!

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:39.200
There, we'll gather our staff, like this.

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.260
Üso?

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:41.330
Yes?

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.330
From now on, no running off on your own!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:48.000
He's got the same expression dad had when he was mad!

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:52.230
Running off on your own is punishable by execution!

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:53.060
Yes, sir!

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:54.430
Grit your teeth!

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:57.560
Clasp your hands behind your back! Spread your legs!

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.130
Lift your head.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.130
Remember exactly what I just told you!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:36.400
When a stranger mentions his father's name,

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:38.930
it's more than Üso can stand,

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:41.600
and now he wants to run from the battle.

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:46.060
And with my heart frozen by the roar of a bombing raid,

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:49.330
all I can do is plant willowherb seeds.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:53.560
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:54.330
Next Episode THE SHRIKE TEAM BULWARK

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:56.830
"The Shrike Team Bulwark".

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:56.860
Next Episode THE SHRIKE TEAM BULWARK

00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:58.030
Please watch it.

00:23:58.030 --> 00:23:59.560
Next Episode THE SHRIKE TEAM BULWARK
